/-!
# Spin-2 AKLT plaquette: completeness of the singlet basis and the leakage map

Builds on `APEX.AKLT.Physical` (five explicit singlets `sv0..sv4`, restriction step
`Intertw Y_ij N_ij`, code `= {c₀ = c₄ = 0}`). Everything is kernel-checked; no `sorry`,
no `native_decide`; finite checks are `decide +kernel` over `ℤ`/`ℚ`.

## Part 1: the five singlets span the whole singlet sector
* `singlet_zero_of_pins`: a vector `φ : V` with `S₊φ = S₋φ = Szφ = 0` and
  `φ(0,4-l,l,4) = 0` for `l = 0..4` is zero. (`Sz` confines it to the 85-dim sector
  `a+b+c+d = 8`; then 80 of the `S₊`/`S₋` equations, in a triangular order found by `peel.py`,
  kill the remaining coordinates one at a time.)
* `singlet_complete`: every singlet `ψ : V` equals `emb c` with the **integer** coefficients
  `c l = ψ(0,4-l,l,4)`, so the singlet ℤ-module is exactly the ℤ-span of `sv0..sv4` (and is
  saturated, so the ℚ-span statement follows too).
* `singlets_eq_range_emb`, `finrank_singlets`: `ker S₊ ⊓ ker S₋ ⊓ ker Sz = range emb`, and it
  has rank 5. This removes the "relative to the span" caveat of `Physical.lean`: the code
  `{c₀ = c₄ = 0}` is `ker H_square ∩ (all singlets)`.

## Part 2: interpretation A (formal combinations of `X_ij^k`): the preprint's numbers
Reduced model over `ℚ`: `X_ij = N_ij / 2` on the singlet sector in the basis `sv0..sv4`
(`Xs`, order `01,02,03,12,13,23`). Coefficient space `ℚ^24`, coordinate `4p + (k-1)` ↔ `X_p^k`,
`k = 1..4` (`ops`, `opOf`). Code projector `Pc = diag(0,1,1,1,0)`, `Qc = 1 - Pc`;
leakage map `leak c = Qc (∑ c_{p,k} X_p^k) Pc`.
* `finrank_range_leak`: `rank L = 6`. `finrank_ker_leak`: `dim ker L = 18`.
* `leak_Cm`: 6 explicit preimages are mapped to the 6 elementary matrices of the `Q·P` block.
* `kb_linInd`, `ker_leak_eq_span`: 18 explicit rational vectors `kb` form a basis of `ker L`.
* `finrank_logicalImageA`: the logical image `{A|_code : A = ∑ c X^k, Q A P = 0}` (the middle
  3×3 block, justified by `logical_spec`) has dimension **4**.
* `leakOp_eq_zero_iff_preserves`: `Q A P = 0` iff `A` maps the code into itself, so the kernel
  does not depend on the complementary projector. Appendix: with the `Gs`-orthogonal projector
  `PG` of `aklt_cert.py` (`gramI_eq`: `Gs` is the Gram matrix of `sv0..sv4` for `G^{⊗4}`, checked
  on all 625 coordinates; `PG_idem`, `PG_Pc`, `Pc_PG`, `PG_selfAdjoint`), the certificate's map
  `leakG` has the same kernel (`ker_leakG`), so also kernel 18 and rank 6
  (`finrank_ker_leakG`, `finrank_range_leakG`).

## Part 3: interpretation B (the generated associative algebra)
* `wordT_linInd`, `span_wordT`: 25 explicit words in `X₀₁, X₀₂` (`wordT_mem`: each is
  `X_g · (earlier word)`, starting from `1`) are linearly independent, so they form a basis of
  `M₅(ℚ)`. `adjoin_eq_top`: `Algebra.adjoin ℚ {X_ij} = ⊤ = M₅(ℚ)`.
* `finrank_ker_leak_algebra`: on that algebra the leakage kernel has dimension **19**
  (rank still 6). `logicalImageB_eq_top`, `finrank_logicalImageB`: its logical image is all of
  `gl(3)` (dimension **9**).

## Which interpretation matches the preprint
The preprint's numbers (leakage rank 6, kernel 18, logical image 4) are those of
**interpretation A**: the 24-dimensional space of *formal* linear combinations of the powers
`X_ij^k`, `k = 1..4`, of the six pair operators (no identity, no products of different pairs).
Under interpretation B (the algebra generated by the `X_ij`, which is all of `M₅`) the rank is
still 6, but the kernel is 19 and the logical image is all of `gl(3)` (dimension 9).

Not done here: the degree-by-degree logical dimensions `1,2,3,4` and the logical Lie algebra
`u(2) ⊕ u(1)` of `aklt_cert.py` are still certified only in Python.
-/

